From a44b3dfc4ec0fb644103b0dbf3473837817b5ed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:25:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] testsuite: fold-round-1.c needs the C99 runtime

The folds fold-round-1.c tests replace a conditional with a new call
to floorf or floorl, which GCC only creates when the target's C library
has the C99 functions.  On targets without them, such as the ELF
targets using elfos.h (no_c99_libc_has_function), the float and long
double functions keep their link_error calls; mips-elf, riscv32-elf,
sparc-elf and microblaze-elf fail the same 8.  Require c99_runtime, as
the builtins tests do.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c: Require c99_runtime.
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c
index 5badefe9c..3897550f4 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/fold-round-1.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /* { dg-do compile } */
 /* { dg-options "-Ofast" } */
+/* { dg-require-effective-target c99_runtime } */
 /* { dg-skip-if "Target lacks hardware-native quad-precision folding routines" { hppa*-*-hpux* } } */
 
 extern void link_error (void);
